#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""lx-deploy: keeps the server on the versions that gzjwyg/deploy's release.json names.

The design is shared-account docs/DEPLOYMENT.md. In short:

- `run` (twice a day, from lx-deploy.timer; or by hand) fetches gzjwyg/deploy with a read-only key,
  accepts release.json only if it names nothing but our own image digests, downloads them,
  backs up the services it is about to change, starts the new versions, checks them, and puts
  the previous versions back by itself if a check fails. It reports pass/fail lines and versions
  (never logs or settings) as a commit status and an issue comment on gzjwyg/deploy.
- It never runs anything from the repository. The compose file, Caddy's files, the timers and
  this program change only when the owner runs `sudo lx-deploy apply-config`, which shows the
  difference and asks first.
- Secrets live only in /etc/lx-deploy/env/ (root, mode 600), created by `init-secrets`.

Standard library only (Ubuntu 24.04's python3). Run as root.
"""

